From: Alexandr Mironov <7062352+alexandr-mironov@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] firmware-xiaomi-vayu: install the IPA firmware

The modem on vayu boots and answers QMI, but ModemManager drops it:

    [base-manager] couldn't create modem for device 'qcom-soc':
                   Failed to find a net port in the QMI modem

The data path runs through IPA, and IPA needs its own firmware. The vayu
firmware repository already carries ipa_fws.mbn and ipa_uc.mbn at the commit
this package pins; package() just never installed them, so the files never
reached the device. Install them next to the other sm8150 images, the way
firmware-xiaomi-raphael does for the same SoC.

The firmware alone is not enough - the IPA node also has to be enabled in the
device tree, which is a separate kernel change. This patch is the half that
belongs in pmaports.

Tested on Xiaomi POCO X3 Pro (vayu_global, M2102J20SG), Huaxing panel.

---
 device/testing/firmware-xiaomi-vayu/APKBUILD | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/device/testing/firmware-xiaomi-vayu/APKBUILD
+++ b/device/testing/firmware-xiaomi-vayu/APKBUILD
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 maintainer="Ali Nasrullayev <nesrullayev.ali@gmail.com>"
 pkgname=firmware-xiaomi-vayu
 pkgver=3
-pkgrel=0
+pkgrel=1
 pkgdesc="Firmware for Xiaomi POCO X3 Pro"
 url="https://gitlab.com/alinasrullayev/firmware-xiaomi-vayu"
 arch="aarch64"
@@ -37,6 +37,15 @@
 	install -Dm644 "$builddir"/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8150/xiaomi/vayu/modem* -t \
 		"$pkgdir/usr/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8150/Xiaomi/vayu/"
 
+	# Data path for the modem. Without these the IPA block stays down, no
+	# rmnet_ipa netdev appears, and ModemManager discards the modem with
+	# "Failed to find a net port in the QMI modem".
+	install -Dm644 "$builddir"/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8150/xiaomi/vayu/ipa_fws.mbn -t \
+		"$pkgdir/usr/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8150/Xiaomi/vayu/"
+
+	install -Dm644 "$builddir"/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8150/xiaomi/vayu/ipa_uc.mbn -t \
+		"$pkgdir/usr/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8150/Xiaomi/vayu/"
+
 	install -Dm644 "$builddir"/lib/firmware/novatek/j20s_novatek_ts* -t \
 		"$pkgdir/usr/lib/firmware/novatek/"
 
